{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121484-modding-the-game-to-add-some-more-d-d-shadowrun-fantasy-elements","id":1121484,"title":"Modding the game [to add some more D&D/Shadowrun fantasy elements]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-27T13:24:43-07:00","id":1121484,"title":"Modding the game [to add some more D&D/Shadowrun fantasy elements]","content":"So I'm trying to come up with a way to mod chronicles of darkness to urban fantasy with more fantasy, like shadowrun but without the cyberpunk elements and more investigation and social stuff. the main issue im coming across is ballancing a party that has some characters with magic some without, the other thing is how do i so the standard fantasy races in CofD and keep them balanced? where should i start?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:39:21-07:00","id":1121495,"title":"","content":"Crossover between more than two gamelines headaches is a pretty massively unbalanced messy affair. Might I suggest Urban Shadows instead, an urban fantasy game that has playbooks for every major supernatural type in the CofD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:47:01-07:00","id":1121502,"title":"","content":"not really what i meant, i like the mechanics of CofD, but im looking for more of a blending of high fantasy and modern, so elves and orcs with machine guns and magic in the big city. thanks anyway, but Urban shadows doesnt really do what i want it to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:18:56-07:00","id":1121533,"title":"","content":"You might wanna check out the mirrors book then. It was first edition, but it had alternate worlds to look at; like one was The Occult States of America, where the masquerade was unveiled, and another where it was in a more high fantasy setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:32:49-07:00","id":1121543,"title":"","content":"What takes on high fantasy races are you thinking of? It wouldn't be too hard to boil down most D&amp;D races to Attribute mods and a free Merit or two. Put those together as packages at an aggregate Experience cost and give everybody some starting Experiences to buy those or other things, and you should be good.<br /> <br /> The other way to do it is do fantasy races as templates, maybe along the lines of the ones in <i>Hurt Locker</i>, but if it were me, I'd want to be able to have dwarf vampires and stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:40:59-07:00","id":1121553,"title":"","content":"yeah the former is probably what i would do, my major problem is what to do with classes (or not as the case may be) and how to do good shadowrun/d&amp;d style magic but balanced with mortals who just have their wits intelligence and maybe a shotgun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:44:30-07:00","id":1121555,"title":"","content":"First reaction: Merits. Lots and lots of merits.<br /> Supernatural race? Give them a bonus merit at character creation that matches their &quot;flavor&quot; (9-again or so on certain skills, and/or bonus dots of skills or attributes, and maybe a free specialty or something; consider a re-fluffed &quot;Professional Training&quot; if you want to really hammer home the effects of their upbringing). If you want those races to matter even more, give each race merit chains that let them build off their base one. Magic? Supernatural merits, and maybe individual powers borrowed from one or two (at most) of the monster lines, converted into individual merits and chains thereof.<br /> <br /> Consider not including a power stat, or making it only affect resistance and whatever fuel you might opt for as a default. If you want to have one, and want it to interact with magic, make merits for your non-magical characters that let them draw on their power stat in certain circumstances, like a &quot;Rage&quot; merit or something. Or just fluff some &quot;supernatural&quot; powers as an extension of their sheer mundane prowess instead of something of mystical origin.<br /> <br /> A good book for this might be <u>World of Darkness: Mirrors</u>. It's a 1e book that covers many different things, sure, but it does spend some time focusing on fantasy hacks. In particular, you could use the book's &quot;Dark Hero&quot; template in part or full as a framework to hang everything else off in terms of powers, and draw inspiration from the sample Dhampir, Atlanteans, and Wargaz for race mechanics. Or as another alternative mechanic for races, borrow the mechanics of the alien &quot;template&quot; from <u>Mirrors: Infinite Macabre</u> to construct the features for <i>every</i> race, including lil old humans (no more of this &quot;baseline race&quot; hooey). Obviously, quite a number of the possible features for that might not work in a fantasy setting (most fantasy worlds I know of don't have playable beings covered in cilia...), so it might be necessary to spitball some tweaks, refluffs, or outright replacements if the remaining features aren't enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 07-27-2017, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T17:21:47-07:00","id":1121626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121484-modding-the-game-to-add-some-more-d-d-shadowrun-fantasy-elements?p=1121553#post1121553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah the former is probably what i would do, my major problem is what to do with classes (or not as the case may be) and how to do good shadowrun/d&amp;d style magic but balanced with mortals who just have their wits intelligence and maybe a shotgun</div> </div> </div> </div>Origin and Role from <i>Bleeding Edge</i> were kinda-sorta designed to bring race and class to CofD.<br /> <br /> For magic... if you want something really D&amp;Dish, you might use Merits to buy spell slots, which you can then dynamically fill with powers based on supernatural Merits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T17:53:55-07:00","id":1121642,"title":"","content":"Check Mage for the Spell Factors (methods of modifying spells to last longer, or include more targets) and apply those to supernatural merits (actually, I've got some notes on doing just that, and I really should get around to posting them...). You can also look into just using some of the &quot;special powers&quot; abilities piecemeal on Mortals and see how that works. Embeds and some Contracts are lightweight enough not to imbalance things too much. Individual Distillations from Promethean's Alchemists are a decent pick. Non-Satiety modified Nightmares might make for good mental powers as well.<br /> <hr /><br /> Actually, if you want to create non-standard Fantasy Races, you could take one power or power line (like a single Vampire Discipline) and make that the race's power. Like a people with inherent Protean shapechanging as their distinct niche, or a group with instinctive use of the Gift of Evasion (either one Facet, all Facets, or the group has sub-types, each corresponding to a Facet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-27-2017, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}